__load("glossary",{"cats":[{"id":"campo","es":"El campo y las zonas","en":"The field and its zones"},{"id":"turno","es":"El turno y la batalla","en":"The turn and battle"},{"id":"invocacion","es":"Invocaciones","en":"Summons"},{"id":"efectos","es":"Efectos y cadenas","en":"Effects and chains"},{"id":"cartas","es":"Tipos de carta","en":"Card types"},{"id":"formatos","es":"Formatos y listas","en":"Formats and lists"},{"id":"jerga","es":"Jerga del meta","en":"Meta slang"}],"t":[{"s":"boca-arriba-abajo","c":"campo","n":{"es":"Boca arriba y boca abajo","en":"Face-up and face-down"},"d":{"es":"Una carta boca arriba es visible para ambos; una boca abajo solo para vos. Los monstruos puestos y las Magias o Trampas puestas están boca abajo hasta que se activan, se dan vuelta o un efecto las revela. Muchos efectos solo afectan a cartas boca arriba, y otros solo a las que están boca abajo.","en":"A face-up card is visible to both players; a face-down card only to you. Set monsters and Set Spells or Traps are face-down until activated, flipped or revealed by an effect. Many effects affect only face-up cards, and others only face-down ones."},"see":["poner","posicion"],"cards":[]},{"s":"campo","c":"campo","n":{"es":"Campo","en":"Field"},"d":{"es":"El espacio de juego de cada duelista: las Zonas de Monstruos (cinco principales y las dos Zonas Extra compartidas), las cinco Zonas de Magias y Trampas y la Zona de Campo. Lo que está ahí está «en el campo»; la mano, el Mazo, el Extra Deck y el Cementerio son zonas aparte.","en":"Each duelist's play area: the Monster Zones (five main ones and the two shared Extra Monster Zones), the five Spell and Trap Zones and the Field Zone. What sits there is \"on the field\"; the hand, the Deck, the Extra Deck and the Graveyard are separate zones."},"see":["zona-de-monstruos","zona-de-magias-y-trampas","cementerio"],"cards":[]},{"s":"cementerio","c":"campo","n":{"es":"Cementerio (GY)","en":"Graveyard (GY)"},"d":{"es":"La zona donde van las cartas destruidas, usadas o descartadas, siempre boca arriba. Cualquiera de los dos puede mirar el de ambos. Muchos mazos lo tratan como un recurso, porque sus cartas pueden recuperarse o activarse desde ahí.","en":"The zone where destroyed, used or discarded cards go, always face-up. Either duelist may look at both graveyards. Many decks treat it as a resource, because its cards can be recovered or activated from there."},"see":["desterrar","campo"],"cards":["Monster Reborn","Foolish Burial"]},{"s":"control","c":"campo","n":{"es":"Control de una carta","en":"Control of a card"},"d":{"es":"Controlás las cartas que están en tu lado del campo y decidís cómo se usan. Algunos efectos cambian el control de un monstruo y lo mueven al campo del rival; cuando esa carta deja el campo, vuelve a su dueño, que es quien la puso en su Mazo.","en":"You control the cards on your side of the field and decide how they are used. Some effects change control of a monster and move it to the opponent's field; when that card leaves the field, it goes back to its owner, the player who put it in their Deck."},"see":["campo","tributo"],"cards":[]},{"s":"desterrar","c":"campo","n":{"es":"Desterrar (destierro)","en":"Banish"},"d":{"es":"Sacar una carta del juego sin que pase por el Cementerio, y dejarla en la zona de cartas desterradas, normalmente boca arriba. Es más definitivo que destruir, porque los efectos que trabajan con el Cementerio no la alcanzan. Solo algunas cartas la recuperan.","en":"Remove a card from play without sending it to the Graveyard, leaving it in the banished zone, normally face-up. It is more permanent than destroying, because effects that work with the Graveyard cannot reach it. Only a few cards can bring it back."},"see":["cementerio"],"cards":["Called by the Grave","Dimensional Fissure"]},{"s":"extra-deck","c":"campo","n":{"es":"Extra Deck","en":"Extra Deck"},"d":{"es":"Una pila aparte de hasta 15 cartas boca abajo con los monstruos de Fusión, Sincro, Xyz y Link (y los de Péndulo, que además pueden volver ahí boca arriba). No se roba: esos monstruos se invocan reuniendo los materiales que cada uno pide.","en":"A separate pile of up to 15 face-down cards holding Fusion, Synchro, Xyz and Link monsters (and Pendulum monsters, which can also return there face-up). It is never drawn from: those monsters are summoned by gathering the materials each one asks for."},"see":["invocacion-de-fusion","invocacion-sincro","invocacion-xyz","invocacion-link"],"cards":[]},{"s":"mano","c":"campo","n":{"es":"Mano","en":"Hand"},"d":{"es":"Las cartas que tenés sin jugar. Empezás el duelo con 5 y robás una al comenzar cada turno. Si al terminar tu turno tenés más de 6, descartás hasta quedar en 6.","en":"The cards you hold and have not played. You start a duel with 5 and draw one at the start of each turn. If you have more than 6 at the end of your turn, you discard down to 6."},"see":["fase-de-robo","fase-final"],"cards":["Pot of Greed"]},{"s":"mazo","c":"campo","n":{"es":"Mazo (Main Deck)","en":"Deck (Main Deck)"},"d":{"es":"Tu pila de robo, de 40 a 60 cartas. Contiene monstruos, Magias y Trampas, pero no los monstruos de Fusión, Sincro, Xyz ni Link, que van al Extra Deck. Se baraja antes del duelo y cuando un efecto lo pide.","en":"Your draw pile, 40 to 60 cards. It holds monsters, Spells and Traps, but not Fusion, Synchro, Xyz or Link monsters, which go in the Extra Deck. It is shuffled before the duel and whenever an effect says so."},"see":["extra-deck","side-deck"],"cards":["Reinforcement of the Army"]},{"s":"posicion","c":"campo","n":{"es":"Posición (Ataque y Defensa)","en":"Position (Attack and Defense)"},"d":{"es":"Un monstruo en Posición de Ataque, boca arriba y vertical, puede atacar y se compara por ATK. En Posición de Defensa, horizontal, no ataca y se compara por DEF. Los monstruos puestos boca abajo siempre están en Defensa.","en":"A monster in Attack Position, face-up and upright, can attack and is compared by ATK. In Defense Position, sideways, it cannot attack and is compared by DEF. Monsters set face-down are always in Defense."},"see":["poner","invocacion-flip"],"cards":[]},{"s":"puntos-de-vida","c":"campo","n":{"es":"Puntos de Vida (LP)","en":"Life Points (LP)"},"d":{"es":"Tu vida en el duelo. Se empieza con 8000 en el formato habitual, 4000 en Speed Duel y 6000 en Rush Duel de Duel Links. Perdés cuando llegan a 0, cuando tu Mazo se queda sin cartas al robar o cuando un efecto declara tu derrota.","en":"Your health in the duel. You start with 8000 in the usual format, 4000 in Speed Duel and 6000 in Duel Links Rush Duel. You lose when they reach 0, when your Deck has no cards left to draw, or when an effect states your defeat."},"see":["fase-de-batalla","coste"],"cards":[]},{"s":"side-deck","c":"campo","n":{"es":"Side Deck","en":"Side Deck"},"d":{"es":"Hasta 15 cartas que quedan fuera del duelo y sirven para cambiar tu mazo entre partidas de un mismo match. Se usa para adaptarte al rival, por ejemplo metiendo cartas contra mazos que juegan muchas Trampas.","en":"Up to 15 cards kept outside the duel that let you change your deck between games of the same match. It is used to adapt to your opponent, for instance by bringing in cards against decks that play many Traps."},"see":["tech","mazo"],"cards":[]},{"s":"zona-de-campo","c":"campo","n":{"es":"Zona de Campo","en":"Field Zone"},"d":{"es":"Una zona solo para Magias de Campo; cada duelista tiene la suya. Si activás o ponés otra Magia de Campo en tu zona, la anterior se manda al Cementerio. Estas cartas cambian el entorno, por ejemplo subiendo el ATK de un tipo de monstruo.","en":"A zone used only for Field Spells; each duelist has their own. If you activate or Set another Field Spell in your zone, the previous one is sent to the Graveyard. These cards change the environment, for example by raising the ATK of one monster type."},"see":["magia"],"cards":[]},{"s":"zona-de-magias-y-trampas","c":"campo","n":{"es":"Zona de Magias y Trampas","en":"Spell and Trap Zone"},"d":{"es":"Cinco zonas por duelista para Magias y Trampas. Las Trampas se colocan boca abajo y se activan cuando se cumple su condición; las Magias pueden activarse directamente desde la mano. En el formato actual las Escalas de Péndulo también ocupan los extremos de esta fila.","en":"Five zones per duelist for Spells and Traps. Traps are set face-down and activated when their condition is met; Spells can be activated straight from the hand. In the current format the Pendulum Scales also occupy the two ends of this row."},"see":["magia","trampa","invocacion-de-pendulo"],"cards":[]},{"s":"zona-de-monstruos","c":"campo","n":{"es":"Zona de Monstruos","en":"Monster Zone"},"d":{"es":"Cada duelista tiene cinco zonas principales para sus monstruos, y además se comparten las Zonas Extra, que tienen sus propios límites de uso. Un monstruo ocupa una zona boca arriba en Posición de Ataque o de Defensa, o boca abajo en Defensa. Con las cinco principales llenas no entran más monstruos en ellas.","en":"Each duelist has five main zones for their monsters, and the Extra Monster Zones are shared, with their own usage limits. A monster occupies a zone face-up in Attack or Defense Position, or face-down in Defense. With all five main zones full, no more monsters fit in them."},"see":["zona-de-monstruos-adicional","posicion"],"cards":[]},{"s":"zona-de-monstruos-adicional","c":"campo","n":{"es":"Zona de Monstruos Extra","en":"Extra Monster Zone"},"d":{"es":"Dos zonas compartidas en el centro del campo, que existen desde 2017. Desde abril de 2020, solo los monstruos Link y los de Péndulo que salen del Extra Deck tienen que invocarse ahí o en una zona a la que apunte un Link; Fusión, Sincro y Xyz pueden ir a tus zonas principales. Genesys no las usa.","en":"Two shared zones in the middle of the field, in the game since 2017. Since April 2020, only Link monsters and Pendulum monsters coming from the Extra Deck must be summoned there or to a zone a Link monster points to; Fusion, Synchro and Xyz monsters can go to your main zones. Genesys does not use them."},"see":["invocacion-link","zona-de-monstruos"],"cards":[]},{"s":"cambio-de-posicion","c":"turno","n":{"es":"Cambio de posición","en":"Changing position"},"d":{"es":"Pasar un monstruo de Ataque a Defensa, o al revés, en tu Fase Principal, una vez por turno y por monstruo. No podés cambiar la posición de un monstruo que se Invocó de Modo Normal o se puso ese turno, ni de uno que atacó. Darlo vuelta es una Invocación Flip, no un cambio.","en":"Switching a monster from Attack to Defense, or the reverse, in your Main Phase, once per turn per monster. You cannot change the position of a monster that was Normal Summoned or Set that turn, nor of one that attacked. Turning it face-up is a Flip Summon, not a change."},"see":["posicion","invocacion-flip","fase-principal"],"cards":[]},{"s":"ganar-un-duelo","c":"turno","n":{"es":"Cómo se gana un duelo","en":"How a duel is won"},"d":{"es":"Ganás cuando los Puntos de Vida de tu rival llegan a 0, cuando su Mazo no tiene cartas para robar al comienzo de su turno, o cuando un efecto especial lo declara. Algunas cartas, como las de Exodia, ganan al juntar un conjunto exacto de piezas.","en":"You win when your opponent's Life Points reach 0, when their Deck has no card to draw at the start of their turn, or when a special effect declares it. Some cards, like the Exodia pieces, win by gathering an exact set of parts."},"see":["puntos-de-vida"],"cards":["Exodia the Forbidden One"]},{"s":"dano-de-batalla","c":"turno","n":{"es":"Daño de batalla","en":"Battle damage"},"d":{"es":"Los Puntos de Vida que perdés cuando una batalla sale mal. En un ataque entre dos monstruos en Ataque, pierde la diferencia el dueño del de menos ATK. Si atacás a uno en Defensa y tu ATK es menor que su DEF, perdés la diferencia; si es mayor, el monstruo se destruye y nadie recibe daño, salvo efectos perforantes.","en":"The Life Points you lose when a battle goes badly. In an attack between two Attack Position monsters, the owner of the one with lower ATK loses the difference. If you attack a Defense Position monster and your ATK is lower than its DEF, you lose the difference; if higher, the monster is destroyed and nobody takes damage, barring piercing effects."},"see":["fase-de-batalla","paso-de-dano","puntos-de-vida"],"cards":[]},{"s":"fase-de-batalla","c":"turno","n":{"es":"Fase de Batalla (Battle Phase)","en":"Battle Phase"},"d":{"es":"Acá tus monstruos en Posición de Ataque pueden atacar, una vez cada uno por turno. Si atacás a otro en Ataque, el de menor ATK se destruye y, si empatan, se destruyen los dos. Contra uno en Defensa se compara ATK con DEF: si el ATK es mayor, se destruye sin daño; si es menor, recibís la diferencia. Sin monstruos rivales, el ataque va directo.","en":"Here your monsters in Attack Position can attack, once each per turn. If both are in Attack Position, the one with lower ATK is destroyed and, on a tie, both are. Against a Defense Position monster ATK is compared with DEF: if ATK is higher it is destroyed with no damage; if lower, you take the difference. With no enemy monsters, the attack goes direct."},"see":["paso-de-dano","posicion"],"cards":[]},{"s":"fase-de-espera","c":"turno","n":{"es":"Fase de Espera (Standby)","en":"Standby Phase"},"d":{"es":"Fase corta que sigue al robo. Por reglas no pasa nada acá, pero se resuelven los efectos que dicen «en tu Standby Phase», como el costo de 700 Puntos de Vida de Imperial Order.","en":"A short phase right after the draw. Nothing happens by the rules alone, but this is where effects saying \"during your Standby Phase\" resolve, such as the 700 Life Point cost of Imperial Order."},"see":["turno"],"cards":["Imperial Order"]},{"s":"fase-de-robo","c":"turno","n":{"es":"Fase de Robo","en":"Draw Phase"},"d":{"es":"Es la primera fase de tu turno: robás una carta del Mazo. Si no podés robar porque no te quedan cartas, perdés el duelo. Quien juega primero se salta este robo en el primer turno de la partida.","en":"The first phase of your turn: you draw a card from the Deck. If you cannot draw because the Deck is empty, you lose the duel. The player who goes first skips this draw on the first turn of the game."},"see":["turno","mano"],"cards":[]},{"s":"fase-final","c":"turno","n":{"es":"Fase Final (End Phase)","en":"End Phase"},"d":{"es":"Cierra el turno. Si tenés más de 6 cartas en la mano, descartás hasta quedar con 6. Los efectos que duran «hasta la Fase Final» terminan acá, y los que duran «este turno» terminan justo después. Luego empieza el turno del rival.","en":"Closes the turn. If you hold more than 6 cards, you discard down to 6. Effects lasting \"until the End Phase\" end here, and those lasting \"this turn\" end right after. Then the opponent's turn begins."},"see":["mano","turno"],"cards":[]},{"s":"fase-principal","c":"turno","n":{"es":"Fase Principal (Main Phase)","en":"Main Phase"},"d":{"es":"Es el momento de desarrollar tu jugada. Podés invocar y poner monstruos, activar Magias, poner Trampas, cambiar posiciones y usar efectos. Hay dos, antes y después de la Fase de Batalla, y la mayor parte de un turno de combo ocurre en la primera.","en":"The time to build your play. You can summon and set monsters, activate Spells, set Traps, change positions and use effects. There are two, before and after the Battle Phase, and most of a combo turn happens in the first."},"see":["invocacion-normal","fase-de-batalla"],"cards":[]},{"s":"ir-primero","c":"turno","n":{"es":"Ir primero y segundo","en":"Going first and second"},"d":{"es":"Quien gana el sorteo decide si empieza o no. Quien va primero no roba y no puede atacar en su primer turno, pero arma su tablero; quien va segundo roba una carta de más y puede atacar. En muchos mazos ir primero es una ventaja, aunque depende del mazo.","en":"Whoever wins the toss decides whether to start. The player going first does not draw and cannot attack on their first turn, but builds their board; the player going second draws an extra card and can attack. For many decks going first is an advantage, though it depends on the deck."},"see":["turno","match-y-side","combo"],"cards":[]},{"s":"paso-de-dano","c":"turno","n":{"es":"Paso de Daño (Damage Step)","en":"Damage Step"},"d":{"es":"El tramo de la batalla en que se da vuelta el monstruo puesto, se calcula el daño y se aplican los resultados. Casi no se pueden activar cartas durante él: solo algunos efectos que cambian el ATK o la DEF, las Trampas de Contraefecto y los efectos que lo permiten expresamente.","en":"The part of a battle where a Set monster is flipped, damage is calculated and the results are applied. Very few cards can be activated during it: only some effects that change ATK or DEF, Counter Traps and effects that explicitly allow it."},"see":["fase-de-batalla","trampa-de-contraefecto"],"cards":[]},{"s":"turno","c":"turno","n":{"es":"Turno","en":"Turn"},"d":{"es":"Cada duelista juega por turnos alternados, y cada turno tiene seis fases en orden: Robo, Espera, Principal 1, Batalla, Principal 2 y Final. Quien empieza el duelo no roba en su primer turno y no puede atacar.","en":"Duelists play alternating turns, and each turn has six phases in order: Draw, Standby, Main 1, Battle, Main 2 and End. The player who goes first does not draw on their first turn and cannot attack."},"see":["fase-de-robo","fase-principal","fase-de-batalla","fase-final"],"cards":[]},{"s":"condicion-de-invocacion","c":"invocacion","n":{"es":"Condición de Invocación","en":"Summoning condition"},"d":{"es":"Una restricción escrita en un monstruo sobre cómo puede invocarse. «No se puede Invocar de Modo Normal» solo prohíbe esa forma: cualquier efecto puede invocarlo de Modo Especial. En cambio «solo se puede Invocar de Modo Especial con tal carta» o «primero se debe Invocar con...» cierran las demás vías, y un efecto no las puede saltar.","en":"A restriction written on a monster about how it can be summoned. \"Cannot be Normal Summoned\" only forbids that way: any effect can still Special Summon it. By contrast \"can only be Special Summoned by such a card\" or \"must first be Summoned with...\" close the other routes, and an effect cannot skip them."},"see":["invocacion-especial","invocacion-normal"],"cards":[]},{"s":"escala-de-pendulo","c":"invocacion","n":{"es":"Escala de Péndulo","en":"Pendulum Scale"},"d":{"es":"El número en los extremos de una carta de Péndulo. Al colocar dos cartas en las Zonas de Péndulo, sus Escalas marcan entre qué Niveles se puede Invocar de Péndulo. También se puede colocar una sola, solo para usar su efecto de Péndulo. Los números no tienen que ser distintos, pero entonces no se invoca nada.","en":"The number at the ends of a Pendulum card. When two cards are placed in the Pendulum Zones, their Scales mark between which Levels you can Pendulum Summon. You can also place just one, only to use its Pendulum Effect. The numbers need not differ, but then nothing is summoned."},"see":["invocacion-de-pendulo","nivel"],"cards":["Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon"]},{"s":"invocacion-de-fusion","c":"invocacion","n":{"es":"Invocación de Fusión","en":"Fusion Summon"},"d":{"es":"Invocar un monstruo de Fusión desde el Extra Deck con una carta como Polymerization, que usa los Materiales indicados, normalmente mandándolos al Cementerio (algunos efectos los destierran o los devuelven al Mazo). Los Materiales están escritos en la carta, por ejemplo «2 monstruos de nombre distinto».","en":"Summoning a Fusion monster from the Extra Deck using a card such as Polymerization, which uses the listed Materials, usually sending them to the Graveyard (some effects banish them or return them to the Deck). The Materials are written on the card, for example \"2 monsters with different names\"."},"see":["material","extra-deck"],"cards":["Polymerization"]},{"s":"invocacion-de-pendulo","c":"invocacion","n":{"es":"Invocación de Péndulo","en":"Pendulum Summon"},"d":{"es":"Colocás dos monstruos de Péndulo en las Zonas de Péndulo. Una vez por turno, podés Invocar de Péndulo varios monstruos de la mano, o boca arriba del Extra Deck, cuyo Nivel esté estrictamente entre las dos Escalas. Con escalas iguales o consecutivas no hay Niveles posibles y no se invoca nada.","en":"You place two Pendulum monsters in the Pendulum Zones. Once per turn, you can Pendulum Summon several monsters from your hand, or face-up from the Extra Deck, whose Level is strictly between the two Scales. With equal or consecutive Scales no Level fits and nothing is summoned."},"see":["zona-de-magias-y-trampas","invocacion-especial"],"cards":["Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon"]},{"s":"invocacion-ritual","c":"invocacion","n":{"es":"Invocación de Ritual","en":"Ritual Summon"},"d":{"es":"Invocar un monstruo de Ritual, que vive en el Mazo, con su Magia de Ritual u otro efecto que lo permita. Tributás monstruos de tu mano o campo cuyos Niveles sumen lo que pida la carta: a veces al menos el Nivel del monstruo y a veces exactamente ese Nivel. No usa el Extra Deck.","en":"Summoning a Ritual monster, which lives in the Main Deck, with its Ritual Spell or another effect that allows it. You Tribute monsters from your hand or field whose Levels add up to what the card asks: sometimes at least the monster's Level and sometimes exactly that Level. It does not use the Extra Deck."},"see":["tributo","magia"],"cards":["Black Luster Soldier - Envoy of the Beginning"]},{"s":"invocacion-especial","c":"invocacion","n":{"es":"Invocación Especial","en":"Special Summon"},"d":{"es":"Cualquier invocación que no es Normal ni Flip: la pide el efecto de una carta, las reglas de un monstruo del Extra Deck o la Invocación de Péndulo. No tiene límite por turno salvo que el efecto lo diga. Es la base de casi todos los combos modernos.","en":"Any summon that is neither a Normal Summon nor a Flip Summon: it is asked for by a card effect, by the rules of an Extra Deck monster or by a Pendulum Summon. It has no per-turn limit unless the effect states one. It is the basis of nearly every modern combo."},"see":["invocacion-normal","extra-deck"],"cards":["Monster Reborn"]},{"s":"invocacion-flip","c":"invocacion","n":{"es":"Invocación Flip","en":"Flip Summon"},"d":{"es":"Dar vuelta un monstruo puesto boca abajo y dejarlo en Posición de Ataque. Los monstruos Flip tienen un efecto que se dispara al ser dados vuelta, ya sea por tu Invocación Flip o porque un ataque los descubre.","en":"Turning a face-down Set monster face-up into Attack Position. Flip monsters carry an effect that triggers when they are flipped, whether by your Flip Summon or because an attack reveals them."},"see":["poner","posicion"],"cards":["Mystic Tomato"]},{"s":"invocacion-link","c":"invocacion","n":{"es":"Invocación Link","en":"Link Summon"},"d":{"es":"Invocar un monstruo Link mandando al Cementerio los Materiales que pide, que suman su Rating Link: suelen ser 2 o más monstruos boca arriba, y un Link usado como Material cuenta como 1 o como su propio Rating. No tiene Nivel ni DEF, no puede estar en Defensa y sus flechas definen a qué zonas apunta.","en":"Summoning a Link monster by sending to the Graveyard the Materials it asks for, which add up to its Link Rating: usually 2 or more face-up monsters, and a Link monster used as Material counts as 1 or as its own Rating. It has no Level or DEF, cannot be in Defense, and its arrows set which zones it points to."},"see":["material","zona-de-monstruos-adicional"],"cards":["Accesscode Talker"]},{"s":"invocacion-normal","c":"invocacion","n":{"es":"Invocación Normal","en":"Normal Summon"},"d":{"es":"La invocación básica de un monstruo desde la mano, boca arriba en Posición de Ataque. Podés hacer una sola Invocación Normal o Puesta por turno. Los monstruos de Nivel 5 o 6 piden un Tributo, y los de Nivel 7 o más piden dos.","en":"The basic summon of a monster from your hand, face-up in Attack Position. You can make only one Normal Summon or Set per turn. Level 5 or 6 monsters need one Tribute, and Level 7 or higher need two."},"see":["tributo","poner","invocacion-especial"],"cards":["Dark Magician","Blue-Eyes White Dragon"]},{"s":"invocacion-sincro","c":"invocacion","n":{"es":"Invocación Sincro","en":"Synchro Summon"},"d":{"es":"Invocar un monstruo Sincro enviando al Cementerio un Tuner y uno o más monstruos que no sean Tuner, todos en el campo. La suma de sus Niveles tiene que ser igual al Nivel del Sincro. Se hace durante tu Fase Principal.","en":"Summoning a Synchro monster by sending to the Graveyard a Tuner and one or more non-Tuner monsters, all on the field. Their Levels must add up exactly to the Synchro monster's Level. It is done during your Main Phase."},"see":["tuner","material"],"cards":["Stardust Dragon"]},{"s":"invocacion-xyz","c":"invocacion","n":{"es":"Invocación Xyz","en":"Xyz Summon"},"d":{"es":"Superponer dos o más monstruos boca arriba del mismo Nivel en el campo para invocar un monstruo Xyz, que tiene Rango en lugar de Nivel. Los monstruos usados quedan debajo de la carta como Materiales Xyz y pueden gastarse para activar sus efectos.","en":"Overlaying two or more face-up monsters of the same Level on the field to summon an Xyz monster, which has a Rank instead of a Level. The monsters used stay under the card as Xyz Materials and can be detached to activate its effects."},"see":["material","extra-deck"],"cards":["Number 39: Utopia"]},{"s":"material","c":"invocacion","n":{"es":"Material","en":"Material"},"d":{"es":"Los monstruos que se usan para invocar un monstruo del Extra Deck. Cada tipo de invocación pide Materiales distintos: nombres o tipos de monstruo, Niveles que sumen, igual Nivel o una cantidad mínima. Los Materiales suelen ir al Cementerio.","en":"The monsters used to summon an Extra Deck monster. Each kind of summon asks for different Materials: specific names or types, Levels that add up, equal Levels, or a minimum count. Materials usually go to the Graveyard."},"see":["invocacion-de-fusion","invocacion-sincro","invocacion-xyz","invocacion-link"],"cards":[]},{"s":"material-xyz","c":"invocacion","n":{"es":"Materiales Xyz","en":"Xyz Materials"},"d":{"es":"Los monstruos que están debajo de un Xyz se llaman Materiales Xyz, o unidades de superposición. Se pueden gastar para activar sus efectos, y si el Xyz deja el campo, los Materiales van al Cementerio. Un Xyz puede ser Material de otro Xyz de Rango mayor.","en":"The monsters stacked under an Xyz monster are called Xyz Materials, or overlay units. They can be detached to activate its effects, and if the Xyz monster leaves the field, the Materials go to the Graveyard. An Xyz monster can be Material for another, higher-Rank Xyz monster."},"see":["invocacion-xyz","material"],"cards":["Number 39: Utopia"]},{"s":"poner","c":"invocacion","n":{"es":"Poner (Set)","en":"Set"},"d":{"es":"Colocar una carta boca abajo. Un monstruo puesto queda en Posición de Defensa, y una Magia o Trampa puesta se activa más tarde. Poner un monstruo cuenta como tu Invocación Normal del turno, igual que invocarlo boca arriba.","en":"Placing a card face-down. A Set monster is in Defense Position, and a Set Spell or Trap is activated later. Setting a monster counts as your Normal Summon for the turn, just like summoning it face-up."},"see":["invocacion-normal","invocacion-flip","posicion"],"cards":[]},{"s":"tributo","c":"invocacion","n":{"es":"Tributo","en":"Tribute"},"d":{"es":"Mandar monstruos tuyos del campo al Cementerio como costo para invocar a uno de nivel alto. Invocar así se llama Invocación por Tributo y es una Invocación Normal, así que comparte el límite de una por turno. Otros efectos también piden Tributo como costo.","en":"Sending monsters you control from the field to the Graveyard as the cost of summoning a high-level monster. Summoning this way is called a Tribute Summon and it is a Normal Summon, so it shares the one-per-turn limit. Other effects also ask for a Tribute as a cost."},"see":["invocacion-normal","coste"],"cards":[]},{"s":"tuner","c":"invocacion","n":{"es":"Tuner","en":"Tuner"},"d":{"es":"Un monstruo con la palabra Tuner en su tipo. Es obligatorio para una Invocación Sincro: el Sincro suele pedir exactamente un Tuner entre sus Materiales, aunque unos pocos piden más o aceptan reglas distintas, y su texto lo aclara.","en":"A monster with the word Tuner in its type. It is required for a Synchro Summon: the Synchro monster usually asks for exactly one Tuner among its Materials, though a few ask for more or accept different rules, and their text says so."},"see":["invocacion-sincro"],"cards":[]},{"s":"activar-y-resolver","c":"efectos","n":{"es":"Activar y resolver","en":"Activate and resolve"},"d":{"es":"Activar es declarar que usás un efecto: pagás los costos, elegís los objetivos y el efecto entra en la cadena. Resolver es cuando el efecto surte efecto, después de que nadie más responda. Entre las dos cosas el rival puede responder, y por eso un efecto puede ser negado aunque ya se haya activado.","en":"Activating is declaring that you use an effect: you pay the costs, choose the targets and the effect goes onto the chain. Resolving is when the effect takes effect, after nobody else responds. The opponent can respond between the two, which is why an effect can be negated even after it was activated."},"see":["cadena","coste","negar"],"cards":[]},{"s":"cadena","c":"efectos","n":{"es":"Cadena","en":"Chain"},"d":{"es":"Cuando activás un efecto, el rival puede responder con otro, y así se forma una fila de eslabones. Al cerrarse, la cadena se resuelve de atrás hacia adelante: el último efecto activado resuelve primero y el primero resuelve último.","en":"When you activate an effect, your opponent may respond with another, and a line of links is formed. When it closes, the chain resolves backwards: the last effect activated resolves first and the first resolves last."},"see":["velocidad-de-hechizo","prioridad"],"cards":["Solemn Judgment"]},{"s":"coste","c":"efectos","n":{"es":"Costo","en":"Cost"},"d":{"es":"Lo que pagás para poder activar un efecto, como descartar una carta o perder Puntos de Vida. Se paga al activar, antes de que el rival responda, y no se recupera aunque el efecto sea negado.","en":"What you pay to be able to activate an effect, such as discarding a card or losing Life Points. It is paid on activation, before the opponent responds, and is not recovered even if the effect is negated."},"see":["negar","cadena"],"cards":["Solemn Strike"]},{"s":"destruir-enviar","c":"efectos","n":{"es":"Destruir, enviar, descartar y devolver","en":"Destroy, send, discard and return"},"d":{"es":"Son acciones distintas. Destruir manda la carta al Cementerio por un efecto o una batalla; enviar la lleva ahí sin destruirla, así que esquiva las protecciones contra destrucción; descartar es mandar una carta de la mano; devolver la lleva a la mano o al Mazo. Los efectos piden una u otra, y no se pueden confundir.","en":"They are different actions. Destroying sends the card to the Graveyard by an effect or a battle; sending takes it there without destroying it, so it dodges protection against destruction; discarding is sending a card from the hand; returning moves it to the hand or the Deck. Effects ask for one or the other, and they must not be mixed up."},"see":["cementerio","desterrar","objetivo"],"cards":["Mystical Space Typhoon","Foolish Burial"]},{"s":"efecto-continuo","c":"efectos","n":{"es":"Efecto Continuo","en":"Continuous Effect"},"d":{"es":"Un efecto que se aplica mientras la carta está boca arriba en el campo, sin activarse y sin usar la cadena, como subir el ATK de otros monstruos. No se puede responder a él, pero otros efectos pueden anular los efectos de la carta, como hace Skill Drain.","en":"An effect that applies while the card is face-up on the field, without being activated and without using the chain, such as raising the ATK of other monsters. It cannot be responded to, but other effects can nullify the card's effects, as Skill Drain does."},"see":["cadena","negar","magia-continua-normal"],"cards":["Skill Drain"]},{"s":"efecto-de-disparo","c":"efectos","n":{"es":"Efecto de Disparo (Trigger)","en":"Trigger Effect"},"d":{"es":"Un efecto que se activa cuando ocurre un hecho, como «cuando este monstruo sea invocado» o «si esta carta va al Cementerio». Si es obligatorio se pone en la cadena sí o sí; si es opcional, solo se activa si cumplís las condiciones de timing.","en":"An effect that activates when something happens, such as \"when this monster is summoned\" or \"if this card is sent to the Graveyard\". If it is mandatory it is put on the chain no matter what; if it is optional, it only activates if the timing conditions are met."},"see":["perder-el-timing","segoc"],"cards":["Sangan"]},{"s":"efecto-de-ignicion","c":"efectos","n":{"es":"Efecto de Ignición","en":"Ignition Effect"},"d":{"es":"Un efecto de monstruo que solo se activa de forma voluntaria en tu Fase Principal, con prioridad, y sin que nada lo dispare. Es de velocidad 1, así que no se activa durante el turno del rival.","en":"A monster effect that you only activate voluntarily during your Main Phase, with priority, and that nothing triggers. It is Spell Speed 1, so it is not used on the opponent's turn."},"see":["efecto-rapido","efecto-de-disparo"],"cards":[]},{"s":"efecto-rapido","c":"efectos","n":{"es":"Efecto Rápido (Quick Effect)","en":"Quick Effect"},"d":{"es":"Un efecto de monstruo de velocidad 2 que podés activar en cualquier momento en que tengas prioridad, incluso en el turno del rival o dentro de una cadena. Las Magias de Juego Rápido y las Trampas también son velocidad 2, aunque no se llamen Efectos Rápidos. Los hand traps son el ejemplo más común.","en":"A Spell Speed 2 monster effect you can activate whenever you have priority, even on your opponent's turn or in the middle of a chain. Quick-Play Spells and Traps are also Spell Speed 2, though they are not called Quick Effects. Hand traps are the most common example."},"see":["velocidad-de-hechizo","hand-trap"],"cards":["Effect Veiler"]},{"s":"eslabon-de-cadena","c":"efectos","n":{"es":"Eslabón de cadena (Chain Link)","en":"Chain Link"},"d":{"es":"Cada efecto que se agrega a una cadena es un eslabón con su número: Eslabón 1, 2, 3... Resuelve primero el de número más alto. Un efecto puede ser negado sin afectar a los demás eslabones, y la cadena sigue resolviéndose hacia atrás hasta llegar al Eslabón 1.","en":"Each effect added to a chain is a link with its number: Chain Link 1, 2, 3... The highest number resolves first. An effect can be negated without affecting the other links, and the chain keeps resolving backwards until it reaches Chain Link 1."},"see":["cadena","prioridad"],"cards":["Solemn Strike"]},{"s":"negar","c":"efectos","n":{"es":"Negar (negate)","en":"Negate"},"d":{"es":"Impedir que algo ocurra, normalmente respondiendo en la cadena. Negar una activación evita que su efecto resuelva, aunque la carta se usó y el costo ya está pagado. Negar una invocación la cancela, y la carta que lo hace suele destruir al monstruo. Anular los efectos de una carta boca arriba, como hace Skill Drain, es otra cosa: la carta sigue ahí.","en":"Stopping something from happening, usually by responding in the chain. Negating an activation stops its effect from resolving, though the card was used and its cost is already paid. Negating a summon cancels it, and the card doing so usually destroys the monster. Nullifying the effects of a face-up card, as Skill Drain does, is different: the card stays."},"see":["cadena","coste"],"cards":["Solemn Strike","Ash Blossom & Joyous Spring"]},{"s":"objetivo","c":"efectos","n":{"es":"Objetivo (target)","en":"Target"},"d":{"es":"Un efecto «apunta» cuando elige cartas específicas al activarse. Si la carta elegida deja de ser válida antes de resolver, el efecto no hace nada con ella. Algunas cartas y monstruos protegen a otros solo contra efectos que apuntan.","en":"An effect \"targets\" when it chooses specific cards on activation. If the chosen card is no longer valid before resolution, the effect does nothing to it. Some cards protect others only against effects that target."},"see":["cadena","negar"],"cards":["Mystical Space Typhoon"]},{"s":"perder-el-timing","c":"efectos","n":{"es":"Perder el timing (missing timing)","en":"Missing timing"},"d":{"es":"Un efecto opcional que dice «cuando» se pierde si algo ocurre después de su disparador y antes de que pueda activarse, por ejemplo si otra cosa resuelve entre medio. Los que dicen «si» no lo pierden. Es una de las reglas que más confunden.","en":"An optional effect that says \"when\" is lost if something else happens after its trigger and before it can be activated, for example if another effect resolves in between. Effects saying \"if\" do not miss timing. It is one of the most confusing rules."},"see":["efecto-de-disparo","segoc"],"cards":[]},{"s":"prioridad","c":"efectos","n":{"es":"Prioridad","en":"Priority"},"d":{"es":"El derecho a actuar primero. El jugador del turno tiene prioridad en cada fase y la va cediendo al rival cuando termina o pasa. Si activás un efecto, el rival gana la oportunidad de responder antes de que resuelva.","en":"The right to act first. The turn player has priority in each phase and gives it to the opponent when they finish or pass. If you activate an effect, the opponent gets the chance to respond before it resolves."},"see":["cadena","efecto-rapido"],"cards":[]},{"s":"segoc","c":"efectos","n":{"es":"SEGOC","en":"SEGOC"},"d":{"es":"La regla que ordena varios efectos de disparo que se activan a la vez. Se arma la cadena en este orden: primero los obligatorios del jugador del turno, luego los obligatorios del rival, después los opcionales del jugador del turno y por último los opcionales del rival.","en":"The rule that orders several trigger effects activating at once. The chain is built in this order: first the turn player's mandatory effects, then the opponent's mandatory ones, then the turn player's optional ones, and last the opponent's optional ones."},"see":["efecto-de-disparo","cadena"],"cards":[]},{"s":"trampa-de-contraefecto","c":"efectos","n":{"es":"Trampa de Contraefecto","en":"Counter Trap"},"d":{"es":"Una Trampa de velocidad 3: la única que puede responder a otra Trampa de Contraefecto. Sirve para negar activaciones o invocaciones, y por eso deciden cadenas que ninguna otra carta puede interrumpir.","en":"A Spell Speed 3 Trap: the only card that can respond to another Counter Trap. It is used to negate activations or summons, so it decides chains that nothing else can interrupt."},"see":["velocidad-de-hechizo","negar"],"cards":["Solemn Judgment"]},{"s":"una-vez-por-turno","c":"efectos","n":{"es":"Una vez por turno (OPT)","en":"Once per turn (OPT)"},"d":{"es":"Un límite de uso. Si dice «una vez por turno», cada copia de la carta puede usar su efecto una vez. Si pide «solo una vez por turno» con el nombre de la carta, es un límite duro: ninguna copia puede repetirlo, ni siquiera otra.","en":"A usage limit. If it says \"once per turn\", each copy of the card can use its effect once. If it says \"you can only use this effect of [card name] once per turn\", it is a hard limit: no copy can repeat it, not even another one."},"see":["efecto-de-ignicion"],"cards":[]},{"s":"velocidad-de-hechizo","c":"efectos","n":{"es":"Velocidad de Hechizo","en":"Spell Speed"},"d":{"es":"Un número del 1 al 3 que ordena quién puede responder a quién dentro de una cadena. Un efecto solo puede responder a otro de velocidad igual o menor a la suya, y los de velocidad 1 no responden a nada. Son velocidad 1 las Magias que no son de Juego Rápido y los efectos de monstruo que no son rápidos; 2, los Efectos Rápidos, las Magias de Juego Rápido y las Trampas; 3, las Trampas de Contraefecto.","en":"A number from 1 to 3 that decides what can respond to what in a chain. An effect can only respond to another with an equal or lower Spell Speed, and Spell Speed 1 effects cannot respond to anything. Normal, Continuous, Equip, Field and Ritual Spells and non-Quick monster effects are 1; Quick Effects, Quick-Play Spells and Traps are 2; Counter Traps are 3."},"see":["cadena","trampa-de-contraefecto","efecto-rapido"],"cards":[]},{"s":"cuando-y-si","c":"efectos","n":{"es":"«Cuando» y «si»","en":"\"When\" and \"if\""},"d":{"es":"En los efectos de disparo opcionales, «cuando» exige que el disparador sea lo último que pasó antes de la activación: si algo ocurre en medio, se pierde el timing. «Si» no tiene esa exigencia y puede activarse aunque pasen más cosas. Por eso los efectos con «si» son más fiables.","en":"In optional trigger effects, \"when\" requires the trigger to be the last thing that happened before activation: if something happens in between, timing is missed. \"If\" has no such requirement and can activate even if more things happen. That is why \"if\" effects are more reliable."},"see":["perder-el-timing","efecto-de-disparo"],"cards":[]},{"s":"contador","c":"cartas","n":{"es":"Contadores","en":"Counters"},"d":{"es":"Marcadores que algunas cartas ponen sobre sí mismas o sobre otras y que otros efectos consultan o gastan, como los contadores Spell. No son cartas ni fichas: se pierden cuando la carta sale del campo, y su cantidad se lleva a la vista de ambos.","en":"Markers that some cards place on themselves or on other cards and that other effects read or spend, such as Spell Counters. They are not cards or tokens: they are lost when the card leaves the field, and their number is kept visible to both players."},"see":["efecto-continuo","magia"],"cards":[]},{"s":"ficha","c":"cartas","n":{"es":"Ficha (Token)","en":"Token"},"d":{"es":"Un monstruo que no está en ningún mazo: lo crea el efecto de una carta y se representa con un marcador. Cuenta como monstruo mientras está en el campo y deja de existir si sale de él.","en":"A monster that is in no deck: a card effect creates it and a marker represents it. It counts as a monster while on the field and ceases to exist if it leaves it."},"see":["monstruo"],"cards":[]},{"s":"flechas-link","c":"cartas","n":{"es":"Flechas Link","en":"Link Arrows"},"d":{"es":"Las flechas de un monstruo Link marcan las zonas de monstruo a las que apunta. Un monstruo en una zona apuntada está «enlazado» a ese Link, y muchos efectos dependen de eso. Dos Link que se apuntan entre sí están co-enlazados. Los Link no tienen DEF: lo que importa son sus flechas y su Rating.","en":"A Link monster's arrows mark the monster zones it points to. A monster in a pointed zone is \"linked\" to that Link monster, and many effects depend on that. Two Link monsters pointing at each other are co-linked. Link monsters have no DEF: what matters are their arrows and their Rating."},"see":["invocacion-link","zona-de-monstruos-adicional","nivel"],"cards":["Accesscode Talker"]},{"s":"subtipos-de-monstruo","c":"cartas","n":{"es":"Gemini, Spirit, Toon, Flip y otros subtipos","en":"Gemini, Spirit, Toon, Flip and other subtypes"},"d":{"es":"Etiquetas junto al tipo del monstruo que cambian cómo se juega. Los Spirit vuelven a la mano en la Fase Final del turno en que se invocan. Los Toon necesitan a Toon World boca arriba y pueden atacar directo si el rival no controla un Toon. Los Gemini se Invocan otra vez desde el campo para ganar su efecto. Los Flip se activan al darse vuelta.","en":"Labels next to a monster's type that change how it plays. Spirit monsters return to the hand in the End Phase of the turn they are summoned. Toon monsters need a face-up Toon World and can attack directly if the opponent controls no Toon. Gemini monsters are Normal Summoned again on the field to gain their effect. Flip monsters activate when flipped."},"see":["monstruo","invocacion-flip"],"cards":[]},{"s":"magia","c":"cartas","n":{"es":"Magia (Spell)","en":"Spell"},"d":{"es":"Una carta que se activa casi siempre en tu Fase Principal. Puede ser Normal, de Juego Rápido, Continua, de Equipo, de Campo o de Ritual. Las Normales resuelven y se van; las Continuas, de Equipo y de Campo se quedan en el campo.","en":"A card that is almost always activated in your Main Phase. It can be Normal, Quick-Play, Continuous, Equip, Field or Ritual. Normal ones resolve and leave; Continuous, Equip and Field ones stay on the field."},"see":["magia-de-juego-rapido","zona-de-campo"],"cards":["Pot of Greed","Raigeki"]},{"s":"magia-de-equipo-union","c":"cartas","n":{"es":"Magia de Equipo y monstruos Unión","en":"Equip Spells and Union monsters"},"d":{"es":"Una Magia de Equipo se activa y queda adjunta a un monstruo boca arriba, dándole un bono; si ese monstruo deja el campo, la Magia va al Cementerio. Los monstruos Unión son monstruos que pueden equiparse a otro monstruo como si fueran una Magia de Equipo y volver a salir.","en":"An Equip Spell is activated and stays attached to a face-up monster, giving it a bonus; if that monster leaves the field, the Spell goes to the Graveyard. Union monsters are monsters that can equip to another monster as if they were an Equip Spell and come back out."},"see":["magia","monstruo"],"cards":[]},{"s":"magia-de-juego-rapido","c":"cartas","n":{"es":"Magia de Juego Rápido","en":"Quick-Play Spell"},"d":{"es":"Una Magia de velocidad 2 que, si la ponés boca abajo en un turno anterior, podés activar también en el turno del rival. Si la jugás desde la mano, solo la activás en tu turno. Mystical Space Typhoon es el ejemplo clásico.","en":"A Spell Speed 2 Spell that, if you Set it on a previous turn, can also be activated on the opponent's turn. If you play it from your hand, you can only activate it on your turn. Mystical Space Typhoon is the classic example."},"see":["velocidad-de-hechizo","magia"],"cards":["Mystical Space Typhoon"]},{"s":"monstruo","c":"cartas","n":{"es":"Monstruo","en":"Monster"},"d":{"es":"Carta con Nivel (o Rango o Rating Link), ATK y, salvo los Link, DEF. Se invoca al campo para atacar y defender. Se divide en Normales, de Efecto, de Fusión, de Ritual, Sincro, Xyz, de Péndulo y Link según cómo se juegan y qué texto tienen.","en":"A card with a Level (or Rank or Link Rating), ATK and, except for Link monsters, DEF. It is summoned onto the field to attack and defend. It is divided into Normal, Effect, Fusion, Ritual, Synchro, Xyz, Pendulum and Link monsters according to how they are played and what text they have."},"see":["invocacion-normal","extra-deck"],"cards":["Dark Magician"]},{"s":"monstruo-normal","c":"cartas","n":{"es":"Monstruo Normal","en":"Normal Monster"},"d":{"es":"Un monstruo sin efecto, solo con su texto de ambientación. Casi siempre tiene estadísticas altas para su Nivel, y sirve de Material o de objetivo para cartas que buscan monstruos Normales.","en":"A monster without an effect, with only flavor text. It usually has high stats for its Level, and it serves as Material or as a target for cards that look for Normal monsters."},"see":["monstruo"],"cards":["Blue-Eyes White Dragon","Dark Magician"]},{"s":"monstruo-trampa","c":"cartas","n":{"es":"Monstruo Trampa","en":"Trap Monster"},"d":{"es":"Una Trampa que, al resolverse, se Invoca de Modo Especial como monstruo en una Zona de Monstruos y cuenta como monstruo mientras esté en el campo. Cuando sale del campo vuelve a ser una Trampa, y no cuenta como tu Invocación Normal.","en":"A Trap that, on resolution, is Special Summoned as a monster in a Monster Zone and counts as a monster while on the field. When it leaves the field it is a Trap again, and it does not count as your Normal Summon."},"see":["trampa","invocacion-especial"],"cards":[]},{"s":"nivel","c":"cartas","n":{"es":"Nivel, Rango y Rating Link","en":"Level, Rank and Link Rating"},"d":{"es":"El número de estrellas de un monstruo. Los monstruos que no son Xyz ni Link tienen Nivel; los Xyz tienen Rango y los Link, Rating Link. El Nivel define cuántos Tributos pide una Invocación Normal y qué Materiales sirven para Sincro y Ritual; en Péndulo, entre qué Escalas entra.","en":"A monster's star count. Monsters that are not Xyz or Link have a Level; Xyz monsters have a Rank and Link monsters a Link Rating. Level sets how many Tributes a Normal Summon needs and which Materials work for Synchro and Ritual; for Pendulum, it sets which Scales it fits between."},"see":["invocacion-normal","material"],"cards":[]},{"s":"magia-continua-normal","c":"cartas","n":{"es":"Normales y Continuas","en":"Normal and Continuous cards"},"d":{"es":"Una Magia o Trampa Normal se activa, resuelve y va al Cementerio. Una Continua se queda boca arriba en el campo y su efecto sigue valiendo mientras esté ahí; algunas piden un costo cada turno. La diferencia importa porque las Continuas pueden destruirse con efectos que apuntan a cartas en el campo.","en":"A Normal Spell or Trap is activated, resolves and goes to the Graveyard. A Continuous one stays face-up on the field and its effect keeps applying while it is there; some ask for a cost every turn. The difference matters because Continuous cards can be destroyed by effects that target cards on the field."},"see":["magia","trampa","efecto-continuo"],"cards":["Skill Drain"]},{"s":"trampa","c":"cartas","n":{"es":"Trampa (Trap)","en":"Trap"},"d":{"es":"Una carta que se pone boca abajo y no puede activarse el mismo turno en que la ponés. Desde el turno siguiente se activa respondiendo a una condición. Hay Normales, Continuas y de Contraefecto.","en":"A card that is Set face-down and cannot be activated the turn you Set it. From the next turn onward it activates in response to a condition. There are Normal, Continuous and Counter Traps."},"see":["trampa-de-contraefecto","zona-de-magias-y-trampas"],"cards":["Mirror Force","Torrential Tribute"]},{"s":"duel-links","c":"formatos","n":{"es":"Duel Links","en":"Duel Links"},"d":{"es":"El juego para celulares de Konami, con reglas aceleradas: Skills por personaje, mazos más chicos y su propio sistema de gemas y cartas. Incluye los modos Speed Duel, con 4000 de vida, y Rush Duel, con 6000.","en":"Konami's mobile game, with faster rules: Skills per character, smaller decks and its own gem and card system. It includes the Speed Duel mode, with 4000 Life Points, and the Rush Duel mode, with 6000."},"see":["speed-duel","rush-duel"],"cards":[]},{"s":"errata","c":"formatos","n":{"es":"Errata","en":"Errata"},"d":{"es":"Un cambio oficial al texto de una carta ya impresa, para corregir un error o arreglar un problema de reglas. Cuando hay errata, vale el texto nuevo en el juego aunque tu copia diga otra cosa.","en":"An official change to the text of an already printed card, to fix an error or a rules problem. When there is errata, the new text applies in the game even if your copy says something different."},"see":["tcg"],"cards":[]},{"s":"edison-goat","c":"formatos","n":{"es":"Formatos retro (Edison, Goat, HAT)","en":"Retro formats (Edison, Goat, HAT)"},"d":{"es":"Reglas y listas de prohibidas de una época concreta del juego, que se siguen jugando por nostalgia o torneos especiales. Goat es de 2005, Edison de 2010 y HAT de 2014. Cada una tiene un mazo y cartas icónicas.","en":"Rules and banlists from a specific era of the game, still played for nostalgia or special tournaments. Goat is from 2005, Edison from 2010 and HAT from 2014. Each has iconic decks and cards."},"see":["lista-de-prohibidas"],"cards":["Mystic Tomato"]},{"s":"genesys","c":"formatos","n":{"es":"Genesys","en":"Genesys"},"d":{"es":"Un formato del TCG lanzado en septiembre de 2025 donde cada carta cuesta puntos y tu mazo no puede pasar un tope, normalmente 100. En lugar de prohibir, hace caras las cartas fuertes. No se usan monstruos Link ni de Péndulo.","en":"A TCG format launched in September 2025 where each card costs points and your deck cannot exceed a cap, usually 100. Instead of banning, it makes strong cards expensive. Link and Pendulum monsters are not used."},"see":["lista-de-prohibidas"],"cards":[]},{"s":"lista-de-prohibidas","c":"formatos","n":{"es":"Lista de prohibidas (banlist)","en":"Banlist"},"d":{"es":"La lista oficial que limita cuántas copias de una carta podés llevar: Prohibida (0 copias), Limitada (1) o Semi-limitada (2). Lo normal es 3. Cada formato tiene la suya y Konami la revisa de forma periódica.","en":"The official list that limits how many copies of a card you can run: Forbidden (0 copies), Limited (1) or Semi-limited (2). The normal limit is 3. Each format has its own and Konami revises it regularly."},"see":["tcg","ocg","genesys"],"cards":["Pot of Greed"]},{"s":"master-duel","c":"formatos","n":{"es":"Master Duel","en":"Master Duel"},"d":{"es":"El videojuego gratuito de Konami, lanzado en 2022, con las cartas del juego físico. Tiene su propia lista de prohibidas y de límites. Las gemas se gastan en sobres y los Craft Points (CP) sirven para fabricar las cartas puntuales que querés.","en":"Konami's free-to-play video game, released in 2022, with the cards of the physical game. It has its own banlist and limits. Gems are spent on packs and Craft Points (CP) are used to craft the specific cards you want."},"see":["lista-de-prohibidas"],"cards":[]},{"s":"match-y-side","c":"formatos","n":{"es":"Match y quién empieza","en":"Match and who goes first"},"d":{"es":"Un match es un enfrentamiento de varias partidas, normalmente al mejor de tres. Entre partidas podés cambiar cartas con tu Side Deck. La primera vez se decide por azar, por ejemplo con piedra, papel o tijera; después, quien perdió suele elegir si va primero o segundo.","en":"A match is a series of games, normally best of three. Between games you can swap cards using your Side Deck. The first game is decided by chance, for example rock, paper, scissors; afterwards, the loser usually chooses whether to go first or second."},"see":["side-deck","turno"],"cards":[]},{"s":"ocg","c":"formatos","n":{"es":"OCG","en":"OCG"},"d":{"es":"El juego de cartas oficial en Japón y Asia. Comparte las reglas del TCG pero recibe productos antes y con otro calendario, y su lista de prohibidas es distinta. Muchas cartas llegan al TCG meses o años después.","en":"The official card game in Japan and Asia. It shares the TCG's rules but gets products earlier and on a different schedule, and its banlist differs. Many cards reach the TCG months or years later."},"see":["tcg","lista-de-prohibidas"],"cards":[]},{"s":"rush-duel","c":"formatos","n":{"es":"Rush Duel","en":"Rush Duel"},"d":{"es":"Un juego de cartas distinto de Konami, con cartas propias y reglas simplificadas: cada carta tiene un solo efecto y no hay cadenas. Llegó a Duel Links en 2023. Sus cartas no se pueden usar en los otros formatos.","en":"A separate Konami card game, with its own cards and simplified rules: each card has a single effect and there are no chains. It arrived in Duel Links in 2023. Its cards cannot be used in the other formats."},"see":["duel-links"],"cards":[]},{"s":"speed-duel","c":"formatos","n":{"es":"Speed Duel","en":"Speed Duel"},"d":{"es":"El modo rápido de Duel Links y también una variante del juego físico. Los mazos son más chicos, de 20 a 30 cartas en el Main Deck, se juega con 4000 de vida y solo hay tres Zonas de Monstruo y tres de Magias y Trampas.","en":"The fast mode of Duel Links and also a variant of the physical game. Decks are smaller, 20 to 30 cards in the Main Deck, you play with 4000 Life Points, and there are only three Monster Zones and three Spell and Trap Zones."},"see":["duel-links"],"cards":[]},{"s":"tcg","c":"formatos","n":{"es":"TCG","en":"TCG"},"d":{"es":"El juego de cartas tradicional de Yu-Gi-Oh! tal como se publica en Occidente, en inglés y otros idiomas. Su lista de prohibidas se actualiza varias veces al año. Lo que ves en este sitio como «TCG» sigue la lista vigente de Konami.","en":"The Yu-Gi-Oh! Trading Card Game as released in the West, in English and other languages. Its banlist is updated several times a year. What this site calls \"TCG\" follows Konami's current list."},"see":["ocg","lista-de-prohibidas"],"cards":[]},{"s":"arquetipo","c":"jerga","n":{"es":"Arquetipo","en":"Archetype"},"d":{"es":"Un grupo de cartas unidas por el nombre o por el diseño, que suelen apoyarse entre sí, como Blue-Eyes o Snake-Eye. Muchas cartas dicen «un monstruo \"X\"» y se refieren a todo el arquetipo.","en":"A group of cards united by name or design, which usually support each other, like Blue-Eyes or Snake-Eye. Many cards say \"an \\\"X\\\" monster\" and refer to the whole archetype."},"see":["engine","meta"],"cards":[]},{"s":"boss-monster","c":"jerga","n":{"es":"Boss monster","en":"Boss monster"},"d":{"es":"El monstruo principal de un mazo, el que querés dejar en el campo al final de tu jugada porque protege tu tablero o se encarga del rival. Los jugadores arman el combo para llegar a él.","en":"The main monster of a deck, the one you want to leave on the field at the end of your play because it protects your board or deals with the opponent. Players build the combo to reach it."},"see":["tablero","combo"],"cards":["Accesscode Talker"]},{"s":"brick","c":"jerga","n":{"es":"Brick","en":"Brick"},"d":{"es":"Una mano que no puede hacer nada útil porque le faltan las piezas para arrancar. Es el riesgo de los mazos que dependen de ciertas cartas. «Brickear» es robar una mano así.","en":"A hand that cannot do anything useful because it lacks the pieces to start. It is the risk of decks that rely on certain cards. \"To brick\" is to draw such a hand."},"see":["mano","combo"],"cards":[]},{"s":"combo","c":"jerga","n":{"es":"Combo","en":"Combo"},"d":{"es":"Una secuencia de activaciones e invocaciones que se enlazan para armar un tablero. Un combo de una carta es el que arma todo el tablero con una sola carta de la mano. Los combos largos se llaman también «líneas de juego».","en":"A sequence of activations and summons chained together to set up a board. A one-card combo is one that builds the whole board from a single card in hand. Long combos are also called \"lines of play\"."},"see":["tablero","hand-trap"],"cards":[]},{"s":"engine","c":"jerga","n":{"es":"Engine (motor)","en":"Engine"},"d":{"es":"Un grupo de cartas, tomado de un arquetipo, que se agrega a otro mazo para darle una función extra, como buscar, robar o interrumpir. Sirve en muchos mazos, aunque hace al mazo menos consistente por ocupar espacio.","en":"A group of cards, taken from an archetype, that is added to another deck to give it an extra function such as searching, drawing or interrupting. It works in many decks, though it makes the deck less consistent by taking up space."},"see":["staple","arquetipo"],"cards":[]},{"s":"floodgate","c":"jerga","n":{"es":"Floodgate","en":"Floodgate"},"d":{"es":"Una carta que cambia las reglas del duelo mientras está en el campo y limita lo que ambos pueden hacer, por ejemplo prohibiendo Invocaciones Especiales. Se usa contra mazos que dependen de combos largos.","en":"A card that changes the rules of the duel while on the field and limits what both players can do, for example by forbidding Special Summons. It is used against decks that rely on long combos."},"see":["combo"],"cards":["Skill Drain","Imperial Order"]},{"s":"hand-trap","c":"jerga","n":{"es":"Hand trap","en":"Hand trap"},"d":{"es":"Un monstruo con Efecto Rápido que se activa desde la mano, normalmente en el turno del rival, para interrumpir su jugada. Se usan para frenar los combos antes de que terminen. Son tan comunes que forman parte de casi todos los mazos modernos.","en":"A monster with a Quick Effect that activates from the hand, usually on the opponent's turn, to interrupt their play. They are used to stop combos before they finish. They are so common that they appear in almost every modern deck."},"see":["efecto-rapido","staple"],"cards":["Ash Blossom & Joyous Spring","Effect Veiler","Nibiru, the Primal Being"]},{"s":"interrupcion","c":"jerga","n":{"es":"Interrupción","en":"Interruption"},"d":{"es":"Una carta o efecto que corta la jugada del rival durante su turno, como negar una activación. Se dice que un mazo tiene «muchas interrupciones» cuando puede frenar varias veces en un mismo turno.","en":"A card or effect that cuts the opponent's play during their turn, such as negating an activation. A deck is said to have \"many interruptions\" when it can stop several things in a single turn."},"see":["hand-trap","negar"],"cards":["Solemn Strike"]},{"s":"meta","c":"jerga","n":{"es":"Meta","en":"Meta"},"d":{"es":"El conjunto de mazos más jugados y fuertes en un momento, y por extensión lo que podés esperar encontrarte en un torneo. Cambia cuando sale una nueva lista de prohibidas o un producto potente.","en":"The set of the most played and strongest decks at a given time, and by extension what you can expect to face at a tournament. It shifts when a new banlist or a powerful product arrives."},"see":["tier","staple"],"cards":[]},{"s":"otk","c":"jerga","n":{"es":"OTK / FTK","en":"OTK / FTK"},"d":{"es":"One Turn Kill: ganar el duelo en un solo turno, dejando los Puntos de Vida del rival en cero. FTK es First Turn Kill, cuando se logra en el primer turno de la partida. Los mazos de este tipo suelen ser frágiles ante las interrupciones.","en":"One Turn Kill: winning the duel in a single turn by taking the opponent's Life Points to zero. FTK is First Turn Kill, when it is done on the very first turn of the game. Such decks tend to be fragile against interruptions."},"see":["combo","puntos-de-vida"],"cards":[]},{"s":"staple","c":"jerga","n":{"es":"Staple","en":"Staple"},"d":{"es":"Una carta que se juega en muchos mazos distintos sin importar el arquetipo, porque cumple una función general: negar, robar, buscar o eliminar. Ash Blossom & Joyous Spring y Called by the Grave son ejemplos.","en":"A card played in many different decks regardless of archetype, because it serves a general purpose: negating, drawing, searching or removing. Ash Blossom & Joyous Spring and Called by the Grave are examples."},"see":["hand-trap","engine"],"cards":["Ash Blossom & Joyous Spring","Called by the Grave"]},{"s":"starter-extender-breaker","c":"jerga","n":{"es":"Starter, extender y breaker","en":"Starter, extender and breaker"},"d":{"es":"Tres roles de carta en un mazo de combos. El starter arranca el combo desde la mano, el extender lo alarga o lo mejora una vez empezado, y el breaker rompe el tablero del rival. Una mano buena tiene un starter, y el mazo equilibra los tres roles.","en":"Three card roles in a combo deck. The starter begins the combo from the hand, the extender lengthens or improves it once started, and the breaker breaks the opponent's board. A good hand has a starter, and the deck balances the three roles."},"see":["combo","brick","tablero"],"cards":[]},{"s":"tablero","c":"jerga","n":{"es":"Tablero (board)","en":"Board"},"d":{"es":"Todo lo que tenés en el campo al terminar tu jugada: monstruos, Magias y Trampas puestas. Un tablero fuerte tiene monstruos que protegen y cartas que interrumpen al rival.","en":"Everything you have on the field at the end of your play: monsters, Spells and Traps. A strong board has monsters that protect and cards that interrupt the opponent."},"see":["combo","interrupcion"],"cards":[]},{"s":"tech","c":"jerga","n":{"es":"Tech","en":"Tech card"},"d":{"es":"Una carta que metés en el Main o el Side para ganarle a algo concreto del meta, en vez de reforzar tu propio plan. Ejemplo: un floodgate contra mazos de combo.","en":"A card you add to the Main or Side Deck to beat something specific in the meta, instead of strengthening your own plan. Example: a floodgate against combo decks."},"see":["side-deck","meta"],"cards":[]},{"s":"tier","c":"jerga","n":{"es":"Tier","en":"Tier"},"d":{"es":"Un escalón de poder para clasificar mazos. Tier 1 son los que dominan los resultados, Tier 2 los que llegan seguido a rondas finales y Tier 3 los que se ven y a veces rinden. Cada sitio los calcula con su propio método.","en":"A step of power used to rank decks. Tier 1 are the ones that dominate results, Tier 2 reach the later rounds often, and Tier 3 are seen and sometimes do well. Each site computes them with its own method."},"see":["meta"],"cards":[]},{"s":"topdeck","c":"jerga","n":{"es":"Topdeck","en":"Topdeck"},"d":{"es":"Jugar con la carta que robaste sin tener otras en la mano. Se dice que un duelo se vuelve de topdeck cuando ambos se quedaron sin recursos y gana quien robe mejor.","en":"Playing with the card you just drew when you hold no others. A duel is said to turn into a topdeck war when both players run out of resources and whoever draws better wins."},"see":["mano","fase-de-robo"],"cards":[]},{"s":"regla-de-nombre","c":"jerga","n":{"es":"«Se trata como» y nombres","en":"\"Treated as\" and names"},"d":{"es":"Algunas cartas dicen que otra «se trata como» una carta con cierto nombre, o que también cuenta como de cierto arquetipo. Mientras eso se cumpla, vale el nombre indicado para los efectos, y el arquetipo se suma al real. Por eso un monstruo puede contar para varios arquetipos a la vez.","en":"Some cards say another card is \"treated as\" a card with a certain name, or that it also counts as a certain archetype. While that holds, the stated name applies for effects, and the archetype is added to the real one. That is why a monster can count for several archetypes at once."},"see":["arquetipo","engine"],"cards":[]}]});